  "articleBody": "Before you jump into installing a stair handrail, it's super helpful to arm yourself with some key questions. First off, how high should your handrail be? Most codes will tell you to aim for somewhere between 30 and 37 inches from the nose of the stair tread to the top of the rail, but sometimes it's closer to 34-38 inches. Then, you'll want to know how many brackets you'll actually need. This often depends on the length of your rail and the material, but don't space them too far apart, or your rail will feel flimsy. It’s absolutely critical to anchor your handrail into studs or other solid framing. Just using drywall anchors isn't going to cut it for something that needs to support weight. Also, consider how far the handrail should extend beyond the top and bottom steps; there are usually guidelines for that to ensure continuous support. Understanding these basics before you start will save you a lot of headaches, and make sure your handrail is not only functional but also compliant and safe. If your stairs are unusually shaped or you're unsure about any of these points, it's smart to chat with an expert like HH Remodeling LLC.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
